  "summary": "Held the entire episode (never fired EXIT). Thesis was intact from the first minute: after a brief -4.5pt dip in the opening 2 minutes, price ran favorably almost monotonically, peaking near +154pts around t=53-54m before giving back to +98.5pts by the window's end at t=60m -- still deeply in-profit throughout, never close to threatening the entry. Against-fires (KMDR/HA/PROPP) stacked periodically during pullbacks but never coincided with a genuine trend break; each pullback was followed by a new high. Next time I'd watch for a pullback that fails to make a new local high within a few minutes AND stacks 3+ against-fires simultaneously with giveback exceeding ~90% of the current leg's amplitude -- that combination never appeared here, which is why this was a clean hold, not a bail."
